// Private Core source part: the zlib kernel (RFC 1950 and RFC 1951) under
// core.archive and the encodings that read compressed bytes.
//
// CRC-32 (ISO 3309 / ITU-T V.42) and Adler-32 return the 32-bit value as a
// non-negative `Int`. `inflate_into` reads stored, fixed Huffman and dynamic
// Huffman blocks; `decompress_into` reads a zlib stream. Both append to an
// empty `out` and answer a status: C_INFLATE_OK, C_INFLATE_MALFORMED,
// C_INFLATE_UNSUPPORTED (past the 64 MiB output budget, or a preset
// dictionary) or C_ZLIB_CHECKSUM. `fault` names a failed status the way
// `ArchiveError` displays it.

C_MASK32: 4294967295

C_MAX_OUTPUT: 67108864

C_INFLATE_MALFORMED: 0

C_INFLATE_OK: 1

C_INFLATE_UNSUPPORTED: 2

C_ZLIB_CHECKSUM: 3

// CRC-32 of each byte value: entry n is n run through eight steps of the
// reflected polynomial 0xEDB88320, so one lookup takes a whole byte.
